From: apklayer
Subject: [PATCH] ANGLE: avoid deferred swapchain allocation on NVIDIA Android WSI

apklayer uses Android's Vulkan WSI to present native buffers to a host Vulkan driver. ANGLE's deferred swapchain path asks Android's loader to create
an unbound VkImage with VkImageSwapchainCreateInfoKHR, whose swapchain handle is owned by the Android loader. The host NVIDIA driver receives this
loader-private handle through apklayer's Vulkan HAL and crashes in vkCreateImage before GLES rendering starts. Use the normal eager native-buffer
swapchain path for NVIDIA when ANGLE is built for Android; keep upstream's existing NVIDIA/Wayland workaround.

--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -6497,4 +6497,5 @@
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
         &mFeatures, swapchainDeferredMemoryAllocation,
         mFeatures.supportsSwapchainMaintenance1.enabled &&
+            !(nativeWindowSystem == angle::NativeWindowSystem::Android && isNvidia) &&
             !(nativeWindowSystem == angle::NativeWindowSystem::Wayland && isNvidia));
